    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Serve Robotics Inc. /DE/ is a public company headquartered in San Carlos, California, traded under the ticker SERV and registered with the SEC under CIK 0001832483. Its website presents it as a maker of self-driving delivery robots, framed around the question of why a 2-pound burrito should move in a 2-ton car. The company describes its offering as a low-emissions solution to the last-mile problem, says it is setting a standard for safety on and beyond the sidewalk, and states that it protects customer data, employees, and the public. It also calls itself a pop culture icon and notes that its robot Saymo appears as John Mulaney's sidekick on the show \"Everybody's Live.\"\n\nThe site's material is promotional and does not name specific products beyond the robot Saymo. No products are tracked for the company, and no MCP servers are listed. No lawsuits are recorded against it.\n\nThe company's recorded location places it in California, a jurisdiction with 281 recorded cases in the site's litigation data.",
